      "19318": {
        "comments": [
          {
            "creator": "kevinushey",
            "is_markdown": false,
            "attachment_id": {},
            "time": "2026-11-14T05:14:40Z",
            "creation_time": "2026-11-14T05:14:40Z",
            "count": 0,
            "bug_id": 19318,
            "text": "When .NAME is a NativeSymbolInfo or an address without registration information, such as the result of getNativeSymbolInfo(\"foo\"), the options(CBoundsCheck = TRUE) errors of .C() and .Fortran() name the routine with uninitialised memory. The R_CHECK_CONSTANTS=5 report of .Call() does the same. Both are there to track down memory errors in compiled code, and the read runs on until it meets a zero byte.\n\nReproducible example: attached as dotcode-routine-name-repro.R (needs a C compiler). It prints, for example, 'array over-run in .C(\"p\\xa9\\xea\"u\") in integer argument 1' where 'array over-run in .C(\"overrun\") in integer argument 1' is expected.\n\nAnalysis:\n\nThe name buffer of do_dotCode() and do_dotcall() in src/main/dotcode.c is filled for a string and, by checkValidSymbolId(), for a registered native symbol. For a bare address it is left unset (r90888).\n\nProposed patch: attached as dotcode-routine-name.diff. It takes the name from the NativeSymbolInfo when there is one and leaves an empty name for an address on its own. make check passes.\n\nThe patch is also submitted as https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/492, where CI results can be seen.",
